{"approved_definition": "Understanding, appreciation, tolerance, and protection for the welfare of all people and for nature. Derives from survival needs that become apparent when people recognize that failure to accept those who are different and treat them justly will lead to strife, and when people become aware of the scarcity of natural resources.", "core_value": "universalism", "sources": [{"entry_id": "5fa8b540:entry:1", "journal_entry": "Went to the literacy camp in Sultanpur today and I keep thinking about this one girl, maybe seven or eight, who was holding the pencil like she'd never held one before. And honestly she probably hadn't. She was gripping it so tight her knuckles were white and she kept looking at me like she was asking permission to write her own name.

I sat with her for almost an hour. The other volunteers were doing group activities but I just couldn't move on from this kid. Her name is Fatima. She got the first two letters right and then she looked at me and smiled and it was like, okay, this is why I wake up early on Saturdays and take that awful bus that takes ninety minutes one way.

I know this sounds naive or whatever. Didi would say I'm romanticizing things. But I was there today and she wasn't. There's something about being in the room with someone who just learned they can write their own name that makes all the other noise—the salary complaints, Baba asking when I'll "move up," the crumbling school building—feel small. Not irrelevant, just not the point.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "5fa8b540:entry:0", "journal_entry": "Parent-teacher meeting ran late. Most parents didn't show up, same as last month. Spent the rest of the evening marking notebooks and helping Amma sort the kitchen.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Making the world a fairer, better place"}

{"approved_definition": "Understanding, appreciation, tolerance, and protection for the welfare of all people and for nature. Derives from survival needs that become apparent when people recognize that failure to accept those who are different and treat them justly will lead to strife, and when people become aware of the scarcity of natural resources.", "core_value": "universalism", "sources": [{"entry_id": "8f83c818:entry:0", "journal_entry": "Had a team standup today and Ravi brought up that our payment processing pipeline is rejecting a disproportionate number of transactions from certain Southeast Asian corridors. The data was right there in the dashboard. Mostly remittance flows, the kind migrant workers use to send money home. Something about the fraud model flagging certain patterns that are just... normal behavior for people sending small amounts frequently.

I knew what I was looking at. I've sat across the table from guys at the worker center who tell me how hard it is to send money back to their families, the fees they pay, the delays. And here's our system making it worse. But when Ravi raised it, the lead just said we'd revisit the thresholds next quarter and moved on. I could have pushed. I had the context, the stories, the data to make a case. But I just nodded and typed something in the chat about checking the logs.

Part of me says it wasn't the right moment, that I need to build a proper case first. But honestly I think I was just worried about being the guy who derails standup with a soapbox moment. My parents always told me not to stick out, keep your head down and do good work. Maybe that advice served them well in a factory town in Fujian. I'm not sure it serves me well here, sitting on information that could change something.", "nudge_response": "Probably something about how the people on the other end of those rejected transactions aren't abstractions. They're the same guys I see on Saturday mornings trying to figure out medical claims. But saying that out loud at work feels like crossing a line I can't uncross."}], "user_phrase": "Making the world a fairer, better place"}

{"approved_definition": "Excitement, novelty, and challenge in life. Derives from the organismic need for variety and stimulation in order to maintain an optimal, positive, rather than threatening, level of activation. This need probably relates to the needs underlying Self-Direction values.", "core_value": "stimulation", "sources": [{"entry_id": "2d928d8a:entry:0", "journal_entry": "Spent the last two hours staring at a term sheet from a Lisbon-based startup that wants us to come in as operational partners. The numbers are solid enough but what actually caught me was the founder, this woman who walked away from a consulting gig to build a port logistics platform from scratch. She reminded me of how I felt fifteen years ago when I signed my first warehouse lease with money I did not really have.

The thing is, I told Ingrid I would slow down this year. We said that after the second exit. That was supposed to be the point where we had enough runway to just breathe for a while. And we do have the runway. But I keep circling back to this Lisbon deal like a dog that will not leave a bone alone.

I know what the smart move is. Park the capital, let the reserves do their work, stay disciplined. But I feel this pull and I cannot explain it rationally. It is not about the money. It is something about the feeling of standing at the edge of something that does not have a guaranteed outcome.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Seeking new experiences and challenges"}

